{"ts":"2026-07-29T16:54:05.041Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"834ed45d6f10ff8b7e7c8f69","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-vv2lti"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Scale fixtures vary only in size: the sole synthetic workspace generator hardcodes population shape, so the million-item tier is eleven simulated days deep with one history entry per item"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The scale benchmark generator at scripts/bench/scale-workspace.mjs is the only synthetic workspace producer in the repository and it exposes exactly two knobs, items and seed. Every other dimension of corpus shape is a hardcoded constant: parent index is the item index minus index modulo twenty, giving a hierarchy of exactly depth two with fan-out exactly twenty; timestamps are the 2026-01-01 base plus one second per item, so the million-item tier spans 11.6 days of simulated project time while the roadmap promises millions of items spanning decades; each item receives exactly one history entry, where the live corpus carries 41,231 entries over 2,204 streams for a mean of 18.7, a median of 14, a p90 of 33 and a maximum of 922, meaning every history-path measurement at the top tier is understated by roughly nineteen times; dependency rows use only two kinds, related on every third index and blocks on every eleventh, where the live graph uses ten kinds including 2,069 implements, 426 blocked_by, 236 discovered_from, 150 verifies and 56 supersedes; there are zero comments, notes and learnings; there is one constant author where the live corpus has 477 spellings; and there are no custom types, statuses, fields, applied profiles or extension-contributed fields. This is a conformance gap against pm-m2il's own fixture criterion, which requires empty and seconds-old scratch projects, representative medium histories, deep and cyclic typed graphs, multi-decade event streams and disconnected archives alongside the size tiers - only the size tiers are producible today. It is also the missing instrument for roadmap horizon Q, which asks which of the product's fitted constants travel to other corpora: that question cannot be answered while only one corpus shape can be synthesized."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:testing","benchmark","conformance","corpus","eval","fixtures","rl-substrate","scale"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-29T16:54:05.041Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-29T16:54:05.041Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":420},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Corpus shape is a declared, versioned specification naming hierarchy depth and fan-out distribution, age span and density, history entries per item, annotation volume, edge-kind mix, author cardinality, and schema customization; The generator produces every fixture shape that pm-m2il's criterion names, including a deep typed graph, a multi-decade age span, a disconnected archive, and a seconds-old scratch workspace, each reproducible from a seed and a shape name; Generated corpora report their measured shape so a benchmark result is attributable to a population rather than to a size alone, and a shape whose measured profile drifts from its declaration fails; At least one published scale, retrieval, and context number is re-measured across two shapes at the same item count, and any constant whose behaviour differs by more than a declared margin is recorded as corpus-fitted rather than universal; The shape specification is reachable from the public SDK so downstream users, evaluation episodes, and domain packs generate their own populations without copying the benchmark script"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-9rxu"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A declared corpus-shape specification drives generation, so scale, retrieval, context and history claims can be measured across populations that differ in shape as well as size."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Only item count and seed are variable; hierarchy depth, fan-out, age spread, history depth, edge-kind mix, annotation volume, author diversity and schema customization are compiled-in constants."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-atfm","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-29T16:54:05.041Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-e5yupa","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-29T16:54:05.041Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-li2fj5","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-29T16:54:05.041Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-m2il","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-29T16:54:05.041Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-mi2x","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-07-29T16:54:05.041Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-o79o","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-29T16:54:05.041Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-o87av6","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-07-29T16:54:05.041Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_sourc